caption: Embodiment of Yin
tradition-component: embodiment-of-yin

Cost: 100 points

Prerequisites: Occult Mastery (High Magic), Yin Master

Requirements: Magery 5, Thaumatology 30

You embody the concept of Yin. Your hair, eyes, and skin become darker, sometimes changing color to blue, gray or black, and your body is cloaked in a shadow that is only visible to those with Magery; this permanently adds your Magery to your Thief-Spy Skills (Stealth, Sleight of Hand, Filch, Pickpocket, etc.). You can never shout. All of your spellcasting, not just High Magic, is now subtle and generates no display, but also takes twice as long (this does not affect enchanting times). You lose all the benefits of Yang Master, if you had that advantage, and may no longer cast using the Yang aspect. Your High Magic using Yin is always free, but only for direct casting (this does not affect enchanting). The duration of your High Magic effects is doubled, and the effective margin of success is also doubled when using trigger-based durations. Enemies suffer a penalty to resist your High Magic resisted direct effects equal to your Magery. You cannot have both Embodiment of Yang and Embodiment of Yin. From a lore perspective, whether someone can embody Yin or Yang is determined at birth, and is related to gender.
